---
/**
 * Get started: the repository's guide (docs/getting-started.md in Clank's repository, the source of
 * truth), designed. The same steps in the same order, with the console's screens beside them and a
 * copy button on every block of commands.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import SubNav from '../components/SubNav.astro';
import InstallCommand from '../components/InstallCommand.astro';
import CommandBlock from '../components/CommandBlock.astro';
import Window from '../components/Window.astro';
import Crop from '../components/Crop.astro';
import { addModel, consent, folder, presets } from '../scripts/crops';
import { GITHUB_URL, INSTALLER_READY, LINKS, PAGES, RELEASED } from '../config';

const sections = [
  { id: 'needs', label: 'What you need' },
  { id: 'install', label: 'Install' },
  { id: 'cloud', label: 'A cloud model' },
  { id: 'local', label: 'A local model' },
  { id: 'folder', label: 'Work in a folder' },
  { id: 'updating', label: 'Updating' },
  { id: 'trouble', label: 'Troubleshooting' },
  { id: 'uninstall', label: 'Uninstalling' },
  { id: 'other', label: 'macOS and Linux' },
];

const repo = RELEASED ? GITHUB_URL : "<the repository's address>";

const needs = [
  ['Windows 10 or 11, with WSL 2', 'everything', 'Docker Desktop turns WSL 2 on when it installs'],
  ['Docker Desktop', "the agent's workspaces", 'each folder you work in gets a container of its own; the first one downloads about a gigabyte'],
  ['uv', 'installing Clank', 'it brings Python 3.12 by itself'],
  ['Git', 'getting Clank', ''],
  ['An OpenRouter account and API key', 'the cloud path', 'free models exist; paid ones need credits'],
  ['An NVIDIA GPU (16 GB is comfortable)', 'the local path only', 'not needed for the cloud path'],
];

const cloudSteps = [
  'Make an API key at openrouter.ai/keys. Add credits if you want paid models.',
  'Type <code>clank</code>. With no model set up, the console opens on <b>Add a model</b> (later: <kbd>F12</kbd> in the menu, or <kbd>a</kbd> on <b>Providers and models</b>).',
  'Press <kbd>c</kbd> for <b>Cloud</b>, then Enter on <b>OpenRouter</b>.',
  'Read the <b>agreement</b>: what goes to OpenRouter (the prompts and the files the agent reads in a workspace you allow), what never goes (Notion, and MCP servers marked local: Space marks or unmarks one), and the data policy (<kbd>o</kbd>). Press <kbd>y</kbd> to agree; <kbd>n</kbd> writes nothing.',
  "Paste the key into the hidden field and press Enter. It is checked with OpenRouter once and kept in Clank's secrets folder only; the console shows its last four characters, never the rest.",
  'Pick a model from the live list: <kbd>/</kbd> searches, <kbd>s</kbd> sorts, <kbd>f</kbd> shows only the free ones. Enter picks it.',
  'Check its settings (filled in for you) and press Enter. Clank sends one short test request and shows the answer and what it cost.',
  '<b>Ready.</b> Clank says whether Docker is running (<kbd>s</kbd> starts it); Enter takes you to <b>This folder</b>.',
];

const folderSteps = [
  'Open a terminal in the folder you want to work in and type <code>clank</code>. The console opens on <b>This folder</b> (<kbd>F4</kbd>).',
  "It lists what working here needs: Docker, the folder's workspace, its software, a model, the gateway. <kbd>g</kbd> does every step that is not done. The first workspace builds Clank's sandbox image, which takes a few minutes.",
  "With a cloud model, Clank asks once whether this folder's work may go to OpenRouter. Answer <kbd>y</kbd>, or keep the folder on your computer only. <kbd>u</kbd> changes it later.",
  '<kbd>a</kbd> starts <b>OpenCode</b> (the agent) in this terminal; leave it with <code>/exit</code> and the console comes back. Or <kbd>c</kbd> opens the folder in VS Code with OpenCode beside your files.',
  'In <b>review</b> mode (the default) the agent asks before it changes a file: answer under <b>Waiting for you</b> (<kbd>y</kbd>, <kbd>n</kbd>, <kbd>v</kbd> shows the change) or in VS Code. <kbd>r</kbd> switches to <b>auto</b>, where it changes files without asking.',
];

const trouble = [
  ['“Docker is stopped”', 'Start Docker Desktop, or <code>clank docker start</code>'],
  ["A workspace says its container uses an older sandbox image", 'Reopen it: <kbd>F6</kbd>, <kbd>x</kbd>, then <kbd>o</kbd>'],
  ["<kbd>F10</kbd> opens your terminal's menu instead of the Monitor", '<code>clank console --page monitor</code>'],
  ['The key is refused (401)', 'Make a new key at OpenRouter and add it again (<code>clank endpoint key openrouter</code>)'],
  ['“No credits” (402)', 'Add credits at OpenRouter, or pick a free model'],
  ['<code>clank</code> is not found', 'Open a new terminal after <code>uv tool update-shell</code>'],
];
---

<Base
  title="Get started · Clank"
  description="From nothing to an AI coding agent working in one of your folders: install Clank, add a cloud model or a model on your GPU, open a folder. Every step, with the commands to copy."
  path={PAGES.start.path}
>
  <SubNav slot="subnav" items={sections} label="Get started, by step" />
  <PageHeader
    crumb="Get started"
    eyebrow="Get started"
    title="From nothing to an agent in your folder."
    lead="Install Clank, add a model, open a folder. The quickest path uses a cloud model through an API key (OpenRouter) and needs no GPU; a model on your own GPU is the other path. Written for Windows first; macOS and Linux notes are at the end."
  />

  <section class="section step-sec" id="needs" aria-labelledby="needs-title">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="num">1</p>
      <h2 id="needs-title" class="h2">What you need</h2>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table class="t needs">
          <caption class="sr-only">What you need, what for, and notes</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">What</th><th scope="col">Needed for</th><th scope="col">Notes</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {needs.map(([what, forWhat, note]) => (
              <tr><th scope="row">{what}</th><td>{forWhat}</td><td class="mu">{note}</td></tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section step-sec" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-title">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="num">2</p>
      <h2 id="install-title" class="h2">Install</h2>
      <div class="soon">
        <InstallCommand id="gs" note={false} />
        <p class="mu">
          {INSTALLER_READY
            ? 'The one-line installer does all of this. To install by hand instead:'
            : 'The faster way, a one-line installer, is coming. Until then, install by hand: it takes a few minutes.'}
        </p>
      </div>

      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          <div class="txt"><h3>Install Git, uv and Docker Desktop</h3><p>In PowerShell:</p></div>
          <CommandBlock label="install Git, uv and Docker Desktop" lines={['winget install --id Git.Git -e', 'winget install --id astral-sh.uv -e', 'winget install --id Docker.DockerDesktop -e']} />
          <p class="mu">Then open Docker Desktop once, accept its terms and let it finish starting. Close PowerShell and open a new one, so the new programs are on its path.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="txt"><h3>Get Clank and install it</h3></div>
          <CommandBlock label="get Clank and install it" lines={[`git clone ${repo} Clank`, 'cd Clank', 'uv tool install --editable .', 'uv tool update-shell']} />
          {!RELEASED && (
            <p class="note">
              <b>The repository's address</b> is shared with you while the repository is private; it is public with the
              first release. Its owner adds you as a collaborator on GitHub first; <code>git clone</code> then asks you to
              sign in to GitHub (or install the GitHub CLI with <code>winget install --id GitHub.cli -e</code> and run
              <code>gh auth login</code>).
            </p>
          )}
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="txt"><h3>Check the computer</h3><p>Open a new PowerShell once more, then:</p></div>
          <CommandBlock label="check the computer" lines={['clank doctor']} />
          <p class="mu">It changes nothing; it says what is ready and what is missing (Docker, WSL, a GPU), each with what to do.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band step-sec" id="cloud" aria-labelledby="cloud-title">
    <div class="container two">
      <div>
        <p class="num">3a</p>
        <h2 id="cloud-title" class="h2">Add a cloud model (OpenRouter)</h2>
        <ol class="list">
          {cloudSteps.map((s) => <li set:html={s} />)}
        </ol>
        <p class="mu after">
          What it costs shows on the header, Home, Requests (<kbd>F7</kbd>), the Monitor and <code>clank cost</code>.
          You can set a daily or monthly limit (<kbd>L</kbd> anywhere, or <code>clank cost limit</code>); when it is
          reached, cloud requests pause until you raise it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="shots">
        <Window title="clank · Add a model">
          <Crop crop={addModel()} label="Add a model: c for a cloud model with your key, l for a local model on this GPU." />
        </Window>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section step-sec" id="local" aria-labelledby="local-title">
    <div class="container two">
      <div>
        <p class="num">3b</p>
        <h2 id="local-title" class="h2">Or a model on your own GPU</h2>
        <p class="para">
          Clank runs local models with llama.cpp or KVMem (an engine that keeps a long context partly in system memory).
          On Windows they run in WSL. This path is not one step yet: the engine is built in WSL and the model file
          downloaded, then a <b>preset</b> (the model with its settings) is loaded into the main slot.
        </p>
        <p class="para">
          Start from <b>Add a model</b> → <kbd>l</kbd> <b>Local</b>: it lists the presets with what each needs and walks
          you through each step, asking first.
          {RELEASED && <span> One setup worth building again, with every setting and why, is written up in <a href={LINKS.models}>docs/models</a>.</span>}
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="shots">
        <Window title="clank · Add a model · Local">
          <Crop crop={presets()} label="Local presets, each with its fit on this GPU and what it still needs." />
        </Window>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band step-sec" id="folder" aria-labelledby="folder-title">
    <div class="container two">
      <div>
        <p class="num">4</p>
        <h2 id="folder-title" class="h2">Work in a folder</h2>
        <ol class="list">
          {folderSteps.map((s) => <li set:html={s} />)}
        </ol>
        <p class="mu after">
          Then look around: the <a href={`${PAGES.features.path}#monitor`}>Monitor</a> (<kbd>F10</kbd>) shows what the
          agent does and what fills its context window, and lets you stop, pause, guide or undo it;
          <a href={`${PAGES.features.path}#flows`}>Flows</a> (F10's Flow view, <kbd>n</kbd>) split a larger piece of
          work into steps, each a fresh session.
          {RELEASED && <span> <a href={LINKS.console}>docs/console.md</a> explains every page and key.</span>}
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="shots">
        <Window title="clank · This folder · F4">
          <Crop crop={folder()} label="This folder: each step working here needs, then the keys to start the agent or open VS Code." />
        </Window>
        <Window title="clank · once per folder, with a cloud model">
          <Crop crop={consent()} label="Clank asks once whether this folder's work may go to OpenRouter: y allows, n keeps it local." />
        </Window>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section step-sec" id="updating" aria-labelledby="updating-title">
    <div class="container two">
      <div>
        <p class="num">5</p>
        <h2 id="updating-title" class="h2">Updating</h2>
        <p class="para">Clank has no update command yet. To update, in the Clank folder:</p>
        <p class="para mu">
          Run these at the computer itself, not over SSH: started from an SSH session, the service runs where it cannot
          use Docker's sign-in. If Clank then says a workspace's container uses an older sandbox image, reopen that
          workspace: <b>Workspaces</b> (<kbd>F6</kbd>), <kbd>x</kbd> to stop it, then <kbd>o</kbd> to open it again.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="shots">
        <CommandBlock label="update Clank" lines={['git pull', 'clank stop', 'clank serve --background', 'clank gateway restart']} />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section step-sec" id="trouble" aria-labelledby="trouble-title">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="num">6</p>
      <h2 id="trouble-title" class="h2">Troubleshooting</h2>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table class="t trouble">
          <caption class="sr-only">What you see, and what to do</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">What you see</th><th scope="col">What to do</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {trouble.map(([see, todo]) => (
              <tr><th scope="row" set:html={see} /><td set:html={todo} /></tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section step-sec" id="uninstall" aria-labelledby="uninstall-title">
    <div class="container two">
      <div>
        <p class="num">7</p>
        <h2 id="uninstall-title" class="h2">Uninstalling</h2>
        <p class="para mu">
          Clank's own folder, <code>%USERPROFILE%\.clank</code>, keeps your settings, records and keys: delete it to
          remove those too. Workspace containers are removed from <b>Workspaces</b> (<kbd>F6</kbd>, <kbd>d</kbd>) before
          that, or from Docker Desktop.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="shots">
        <CommandBlock label="uninstall Clank" lines={['clank stop', 'uv tool uninstall clank']} />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section step-sec" id="other" aria-labelledby="other-title">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 id="other-title" class="h2">macOS and Linux</h2>
      <p class="para wide">
        Clank's console, the cloud path and its commands are the same; install uv, Git and Docker (Docker Desktop on
        macOS; Docker Engine on Linux) the way your system does, then follow step 2 from <code>git clone</code>. Neither
        has been tested yet. On Linux, the agent's container reaching Clank's gateway through Docker Engine is still
        being built, so the agent may not reach the model there yet.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  section[id] {
    scroll-margin-top: 120px;
  }

  .step-sec {
    padding-top: clamp(64px, 7vw, 104px);
  }

  .num {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--orange);
  }

  .h2 {
    margin-top: 6px;
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 1.25rem + 1.5vw, 2.25rem);
    line-height: 1.12;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .mu {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .para {
    margin-top: 14px;
    max-width: 44rem;
  }

  .para.wide {
    max-width: 52rem;
  }

  .table-wrap {
    margin-top: 22px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .t {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .t th,
  .t td {
    padding: 13px 18px;
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .t thead th {
    border-top: 0;
    background: var(--surface);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .t tbody th {
    color: var(--text-strong);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .needs tbody th {
    width: 32%;
  }

  .trouble tbody th {
    width: 45%;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .soon {
    margin-top: 22px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
    max-width: 40rem;
  }

  .steps {
    margin-top: 32px;
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: s;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 28px;
    max-width: 46rem;
  }

  .steps > li {
    counter-increment: s;
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
    padding-left: 46px;
  }

  .steps > li::before {
    content: counter(s);
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 30px;
    height: 30px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text-strong);
  }

  .txt {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
  }

  .txt h3 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .note {
    padding: 12px 16px;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--yellow) 35%, transparent);
    background: rgba(224, 175, 104, 0.05);
    border-radius: 10px;
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .note b {
    color: var(--text-strong);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .two {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 32px clamp(32px, 5vw, 64px);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .list {
    margin-top: 20px;
    padding-left: 1.5em;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .list li::marker {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--orange);
  }

  .list :global(b),
  .para b {
    color: var(--text-strong);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .list :global(code),
  .para code,
  .after code,
  .note code,
  .t :global(code) {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.88em;
    padding: 0.08em 0.35em;
    border-radius: 5px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: var(--surface-2);
    color: var(--text-strong);
  }

  .list :global(kbd),
  .para kbd,
  .after kbd,
  .t :global(kbd) {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.82em;
    padding: 0.05em 0.4em;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    border-bottom-width: 2px;
    border-radius: 5px;
    background: var(--surface-2);
    color: var(--text-strong);
  }

  .after {
    margin-top: 18px;
  }

  .shots {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 18px;
    min-width: 0;
    position: sticky;
    top: 140px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .two {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .shots {
      position: static;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .t thead {
      display: none;
    }

    .t tr {
      display: grid;
      gap: 4px;
      padding: 12px 14px;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    }

    .t tbody tr:first-child {
      border-top: 0;
    }

    .t th,
    .t td {
      display: block;
      width: auto !important;
      padding: 0;
      border: 0;
    }

    .steps > li {
      padding-left: 40px;
    }
  }
</style>
